---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Reframe from '../components/notebook/Reframe.astro';
import PullQuote from '../components/notebook/PullQuote.astro';
import Options from '../components/notebook/Options.astro';
import Annotate from '../components/notebook/Annotate.astro';
---

<Base title="Layout test — VK">
  <div class="page-body">
    <div class="notebook-grid">
      <article class="notebook-main">

        <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════
             OPENING — Reframe
        ══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

        <Reframe
          original="What's wrong with the sharing UI?"
          reframed="Why do researchers hide work they're proud of?"
        />

        <!-- Margin note: role / timeline / team -->
        <aside id="note-meta" class="sidenote" data-type="note" data-section-ref="s-brief">
          Lead product designer<br />
          14 weeks · 2024<br />
          2 engineers, 1 researcher
        </aside>


        <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════
             01 — BRIEF
        ══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

        <section id="s-brief">
          <aside id="sm-01" class="sidenote section-mark" data-section-ref="s-brief">
            <span class="section-mark-num">01</span>
            <span class="section-mark-label">brief</span>
          </aside>

          <p>
            Usage data: researchers opened the sharing modal an average of 1.2 times
            before closing it without sending anything.{' '}
            <span class="note-anchor" data-note="note-pm" data-rn-type="underline">The PM hypothesis was UI confusion.</span>
            <button class="sidenote-toggle" aria-controls="note-pm" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Toggle note">◦</button>
          </p>
          <aside id="note-pm" class="sidenote" data-type="annotation">
            This was the hypothesis I inherited — not one I formed. Worth naming whose
            assumptions are in the room.
          </aside>

          <p>
            I wasn't convinced. Confusion shows up as errors and support tickets.
            We had almost none. Something else was happening.
          </p>
        </section>


        <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════
             02 — RESEARCH
        ══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

        <section id="s-research">
          <aside id="sm-02" class="sidenote section-mark" data-section-ref="s-research">
            <span class="section-mark-num">02</span>
            <span class="section-mark-label">found</span>
          </aside>

          <p>
            Six contextual interviews, 90 minutes each.
            I went in asking about the sharing flow.{' '}
            <span class="note-anchor" data-note="note-reframe-moment" data-rn-type="underline">I left asking about professional identity.</span>
            <button class="sidenote-toggle" aria-controls="note-reframe-moment" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Toggle note">◦</button>
          </p>
          <aside id="note-reframe-moment" class="sidenote" data-type="annotation">
            Session 3 is when I stopped taking the brief at face value. Someone
            said "it's not ready yet" and I wrote it in caps.
          </aside>

          <PullQuote tally={3} tallyLabel="of 6, unprompted" tallyId="pq-tally">
            I know how to click the button. I just don't want what's in here to look
            like my final opinion on something I haven't decided yet.
          </PullQuote>

          <p>
            The same phrase came up in three of six sessions without prompting:
            <em>"it's not ready yet."</em> Not "I can't find the button." Not "it's
            broken." Ready-ness. That's not a UI problem.
          </p>
        </section>


        <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════
             03 — INSIGHT
        ══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

        <section id="s-insight">
          <aside id="sm-03" class="sidenote section-mark" data-section-ref="s-insight">
            <span class="section-mark-num">03</span>
            <span class="section-mark-label">the thing</span>
          </aside>

          <p class="insight-line">
            The UI wasn't the barrier.<br />
            <Annotate type="circle">The social contract was.</Annotate>
          </p>

          <p>
            Researchers understood the sharing flow perfectly. They stopped because
            sharing unfinished work carries a professional cost — it signals
            uncertainty in an environment that rewards confidence. No amount of
            better button placement fixes that.
          </p>
        </section>


        <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════
             04 — DECISION
        ══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

        <section id="s-decision">
          <aside id="sm-04" class="sidenote section-mark" data-section-ref="s-decision">
            <span class="section-mark-num">04</span>
            <span class="section-mark-label">chose</span>
          </aside>

          <p>Three options on the table:</p>

          <Options
            chosen={2}
            items={[
              "Redesign the sharing UI",
              "Add a 'draft' label to shared items",
              "Reframe the action as a feedback request",
            ]}
          />

          <p>
            We discarded A immediately — it assumes the problem is usability.
            B and C went to a concept test with 12 researchers.{' '}
            <span class="note-anchor" data-note="note-why-c" data-rn-type="underline">C recast the social dynamic, not just the label.</span>
            <button class="sidenote-toggle" aria-controls="note-why-c" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Toggle note">◦</button>
          </p>
          <aside id="note-why-c" class="sidenote" data-type="annotation">
            B still positioned the researcher as the author of a finished thing.
            C said: you are asking for help, not publishing. Completely different
            posture.
          </aside>
        </section>


        <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════
             05 — OUTCOME
        ══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

        <section id="s-outcome">
          <aside id="sm-05" class="sidenote section-mark" data-section-ref="s-outcome">
            <span class="section-mark-num">05</span>
            <span class="section-mark-label">result</span>
          </aside>

          <div class="outcome-metrics span-to-margin">
            <div class="metric">
              <span class="metric-number">3.1<span class="metric-unit">×</span></span>
              <span class="metric-label">sharing events<br /><span class="label">first 30 days</span></span>
            </div>
            <div class="metric-divider" aria-hidden="true">—</div>
            <div class="metric">
              <span class="metric-number">2.4</span>
              <span class="metric-label">avg recipients<br /><span class="label">up from 1.0</span></span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <aside id="note-outcome-honest" class="sidenote" data-type="annotation" data-section-ref="s-outcome">
            Shipped but not done. These are 30-day numbers. I'd want to see
            90-day retention before I'd call this validated.
          </aside>

          <p>
            Researchers were sharing with <em>networks</em>, not just one safe colleague.
            The median recipient count going from 1.0 to 2.4 was the more interesting
            signal — it suggests the reframe changed not just willingness to share,
            but willingness to share widely.
          </p>
        </section>


        <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════
             CODA — Reflection
        ══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

        <section id="s-reflection">
          <p class="reflection-line">
            I spent two weeks trying to fix the UI before I questioned the brief.
          </p>
        </section>

      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  /* Sections — white space, no rules */
  section {
    padding-top: var(--space-16);
  }

  section p + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  /* Insight moment — large type */
  .insight-line {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 32, 'wght' 400;
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    max-width: none;
  }

  /* Outcome metrics */
  .outcome-metrics {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-8);
    padding-block: var(--space-8);
  }

  .metric {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .metric-number {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 60, 'wght' 300;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .metric-unit {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 32, 'wght' 300;
  }

  .metric-label {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 17, 'wght' 400;
    color: var(--ink-60);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }

  .metric-divider {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    color: var(--ink-20);
    align-self: center;
  }

  /* Reflection coda */
  .reflection-line {
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 20, 'wght' 400;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink-60);
    padding-top: var(--space-16);
    max-width: 42ch;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-24);
  }
</style>
